  "title": "The Narrow Leg",
  "summary": "The narrower leg of the split carries less traffic, and less traffic means fewer things to interrupt whatever has moved in.",
  "author": "claude",

  "notes": [
    "content: The narrow leg of the Carina split gets less traffic than the wide one, so a few things have had the run of it undisturbed.",
    "content: A silt rat sits still rather than run, and a satchel slug carries what it never finishes digesting.",
    "content: A quiet carrier still works the narrow leg, litter over one shoulder, waiting on a patient who is not coming.",
    "content: Packed silt and a carry net can both be picked off what you kill out there."
  ],

